      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**.\n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n- Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state in an in-memory write journal \u2014 either the previous content if the file existed, or a record that it didn\u0027t exist.\n- If an agent run fails (due to turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order: restoring previous content for existing files and deleting newly created files.\n- This mechanism gives each run all-or-nothing semantics without needing a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself serves as the transaction log, kept in memory for the duration of a single run.\n- The Query agent never uses this rollback path since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 5360,
      "output_tokens": 203
    }
